<p>I have to admit a certain disappointment. The punchline to this seems to be a completely different SCP. Like, there's not an actual anomaly here, it's just a place that leads you to where something already documented happens.</p>
<p>That said, I agree with kaktus that the writing is solid and the dialogue strong. And watching the interviewer slowly lose his understanding of what's going on while the Sgt. is unaffected was pretty damned creepy.</p>

